        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm recalling that ष्मिङ् belongs to the churadi gana meaning अनादरे (disrespect/disregard), listed among the आकुस्मीयाः atmanepadi roots alongside चित्, and tracing its causative form स्माय.\n\nWorking through the णिच् derivation, स्मि becomes स्माय via vriddhi, giving स्माययते, with periphrastic perfect forms स्माययाञ्चक्राते, स्माययाम्बभूवतुः, and स्माययामासतुः for dual third person, since कृञ् follows the atmanepada of the preceding dhatu. I'm also double-checking this against the bhvadi स्मिङ् (ईषद्धसने) which under rule 6.1.57 नित्यं स्मयतेः takes a different causative path (विस्मापयते) only in the हेतुभय context, confirming the churadi root's forms are distinct — स्माययते as per the Siddhanta Kaumudi.\n\n",
